    "result_text": "BUILD SUCCESS \u2014 the test passes. The audit output confirms the behavior: `memberId=NSWV22716E6609E7` (V2-tagged region inside the identifier), `\"schemaVersion\":2`, `\"ownerSegment\":\"STANDARD_METRO\"`, while `locality` stays the plain region.\n\n## Summary\n\nReleased version 2 of the owner identity. Changes were kept as small, cohesive edits in low-complexity classes:\n\n**Version-2 identity derivation** (each identifier now mixes a fixed `V2` tag, so every value changes and no v1 value recurs):\n- `util/IdentityKeys.java` \u2014 hashed input now prefixed `\"V2|\"`.\n- `rest/controller/v1/Households.java` \u2014 `householdId` hash input prefixed `\"V2|\"`.\n- `util/MemberIds.java` \u2014 the region code *inside* the memberId is tagged (`NSW` \u2192 `NSWV2`), so `memberId` changes.\n\n**User-facing fields stay plain** (V2 tag never leaks out): `locality`, `timezone`, and the owner segment's region still read `CustomerCodes.regionOf(customerCode)` \u2014 unchanged.\n\n**Response shape**:\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; added a nested `OwnerIdentity` schema (`identity` object) holding the three, plus a top-level integer `apiVersion`.\n- `mapper/OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 added `apiVersion` = 2 and an `identity` mapping via a small `toOwnerIdentity(owner)` default method; dropped the two top-level identity mappings.\n\n**Audit event** (`model/OwnerAuditListener.java`):\n- Structured event moved to schema version 2 \u2014 added `\"schemaVersion\":2` and an `\"ownerSegment\"` recomputed from the (v2) membership level and the plain region.\n\nRequest fields (`OwnerFields`) are untouched. Test suite: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 green.",
