    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list for `POST /api/owners`. That path is served by `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` (the class is `@RequestMapping(\"/api\")` and implements `OwnersApi`, whose `addOwner` maps `POST /owners`; the v2 controller only adds a paged GET). Steps are in the exact order they execute. **[V]** = a validation that can reject the request; **[S]** = a side-effect (mutation, persistence, or log).\n\n## Stage 0 \u2014 Security (before the method runs)\n1. **[V]** `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` \u2014 the caller must hold the `OWNER_ADMIN` role, else 403.\n\n## Stage 1 \u2014 Bean Validation on `@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` (before the body runs; any failure \u2192 400)\nField-level constraints:\n2. **[V]** `firstName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}$` (letters, up to two space/'/- separated parts).\n3. **[V]** `lastName` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern ^[\\p{L}]+([ '-][\\p{L}]+){0,2}\\.?$` (same, optional trailing dot).\n4. **[V]** `title` \u2014 `@Size(max 10)` (optional).\n5. **[V]** `address` \u2014 `@Pattern .*\\S.*` (non-blank), `@Size(1..255)` (optional).\n6. **[V]** `addressLine1` \u2014 `@Pattern .*\\S.*`, `@Size(1..255)` (optional).\n7. **[V]** `addressLine2` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)` (optional).\n8. **[V]** `city` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Pattern .*\\S.*`, `@Size(1..80)`.\n9. **[V]** `telephone` \u2014 `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`, `@Pattern ^\\D*(\\d\\D*){10}$` (exactly 10 digits after non-digits are ignored).\n10. **[V]** `email` \u2014 `@Size(max 255)`, `@Email` (optional).\n11. **[V]** `registrationDate` \u2014 `@PastOrPresent` (optional; cannot be in the future).\n12. **[V]** `postcode` \u2014 `@Pattern ^[0-9]{4}$` (optional).\n\nClass-level constraints on the whole DTO:\n13. **[V]** `@AddressPresenceValidation` \u2014 at least one of `addressLine1` or `address` must be non-blank.\n14. **[V]** `@PostcodeValidation` \u2014 if a 4-digit `postcode` is present **and** the city maps to a known region (`Localities.regionOf(city)` \u2192 NSW/VIC/QLD), the postcode must fall in that region's inclusive range (NSW 2000\u20132099, VIC 3000\u20133099, QLD 4000\u20134099). Unknown city or absent postcode passes.\n\n## Stage 2 \u2014 Mapping DTO \u2192 `Owner` (`ownerMapper.toOwner`)\n15. **[S]** `id` and `pets` ignored; a fresh transient `Owner` is built.\n16. **[S/V]** `telephone` normalized to E.164 via `E164.toE164` (strips non-digits; assumes Australia when no leading `+` \u2014 prepends `61`, drops a leading `0`). Throws `IllegalArgumentException` on invalid national length \u2014 a soft validation that would surface as a 500 rather than a clean 400.\n17. **[S]** `addressLine1`/`addressLine2` normalized via `Addresses.normalize` (trim, upper-case, collapse whitespace, expand `ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`).\n18. **[S]** `address` composed via `Addresses.compose` \u2014 prefers normalized `addressLine1` (+ line2), else the normalized flat `address`.\n19. **[S]** `email` stored lower-cased (`Owner.setEmail`).\n\n## Stage 3 \u2014 Business-rule checks in the controller body (each can short-circuit before any save)\n20. **[V]** `DisposableDomains.isBlocked(owner)` \u2014 email domain in the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) \u2192 **400 BAD_REQUEST**.\n21. **[S]** Loads all owners once via `clinicService.findAllOwners()` (used by the checks below).\n22. **[V]** `DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, today) >= 100` \u2192 **429 TOO_MANY_REQUESTS** (owners already registered for today's rolled-forward business day).\n23. **[V]** `CityCodes.count(owners, owner) >= 50` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT** (per-city cap; case-insensitive city match).\n24. **[S]** `owner.setHouseholdId(Households.householdId(owner))` \u2014 transient household id = first 12 chars of `sha256(\"V2|\"+normalized lastName+\"|\"+postcode)`.\n25. **[V]** `IdentityKeys.isDuplicate(owners, owner)` \u2192 **409 CONFLICT** \u2014 duplicate if any **non-deleted** owner shares the identity key `sha256(\"V2|\"+telephone+\"|\"+lowerEmail+\"|\"+soundex(lastName))`.\n\n## Stage 4 \u2014 Deriving transient/enrichment fields (side-effects on the owner before save)\n26. **[S]** `owner.setBulkSignupWarning(DailyRegistrations.countOn(owners, today) > 80)` \u2014 transient warning flag.\n27. **[S]** `owner.setNamesakeCount(Namesakes.count(owners, owner))` \u2014 transient count of owners with same first+last name.\n28. **[S]** `owner.setCustomerCode(UniqueCustomerCodes.deduplicate(owners, CustomerCodes.of(owner)))` \u2014 assigns customer code `<REGION>-<HASH8>` (region from city+postcode; hash8 of telephone+lastName), suffixing `-2`, `-3`, \u2026 if that code is already taken.\n\n## Stage 5 \u2014 Persistence (`clinicService.saveOwner` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save`, within `@Transactional`)\n29. **[S]** `@PrePersist ensureRegistrationDate()` \u2014 defaults `registrationDate` to today if null, then rolls it forward to the next business day (`BusinessDays.rollForward`, skipping weekends and the fixed 2026 holidays).\n30. **[V]** Entity-level Bean Validation at flush \u2014 `Owner`: `@NotEmpty address`, `@NotEmpty city`, `@NotEmpty`/`@Pattern ^\\+[0-9]{8,15}$ telephone`; `Person`: `@NotEmpty firstName`, `@NotEmpty lastName`. (These re-check the normalized entity state at persist time.)\n31. **[S]** INSERT into `owners` (with `deleted = false`).\n32. **[S]** `@PostPersist OwnerAuditListener.onCreate(owner)` \u2014 computes `memberId` (`MemberIds.of`), `membershipLevel`, and `ownerSegment`; then emits: one `NOTIFY` \"welcome owner\" log line and two `AUDIT` log lines (a human-readable one and a JSON `OWNER_CREATED` event carrying an incrementing sequence number).\n\n## Stage 6 \u2014 Response assembly\n33. **[S]** `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto(owner)` computes response-only derived fields (selfLink, displayName, salutation, initials, apiVersion, identity block `{memberId, identityKey, householdId}`, fiscalYear, membershipPoints/level, locality, ownerSegment, timezone, contactPreference, telephoneDisplay) \u2014 not persisted.\n34. **[S]** Sets `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header.\n35. **[S]** Returns **201 CREATED** with the owner body.\n\nA couple of things worth flagging: the duplicate/cap checks vary in whether they exclude soft-deleted owners \u2014 only `IdentityKeys.isDuplicate` (the 409 identity check) skips `deleted` owners, whereas `DailyRegistrations`, `CityCodes`, and `Namesakes` count all rows including deleted ones. Also note `Owner.assignCustomerCode(int)` exists but is **not** used on this path \u2014 the code is assigned via `UniqueCustomerCodes.deduplicate` at step 28 instead."
